.TH sandogasa-report 1 2026-11-20 "sandogasa 0.28.2" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
sandogasa\-report \- Activity reporting for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIG packaging work
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsandogasa\-report\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Activity reporting for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIG packaging work
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS sandogasa-report config
\fBsandogasa\-report config\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-missing\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Interactively set per\-user overrides in `~/.config/sandogasa\-report/config.toml`
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Also go over the instances whose token is turned off ("\-"), offering the keyring\*(Aqs again where it has one
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Main config file to enumerate domains / forge instances from. Without one, there are no instances to configure
.TP
\fB\-\-missing\fR
Ask only for what is not set yet: a field with a value, and an instance with a token, are kept as they are, unchecked
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<HOST>\fR
Ask again only for the token kept for HOST (e.g. forge.fedoraproject.org, or its URL), even though one is saved; Enter keeps it. May be given more than once
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS sandogasa-report note
\fBsandogasa\-report note\fR [\fB\-\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-date\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITEXT\fR>
.PP
Record a note on why a piece of work was done
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Who wrote the text, when not you (e.g. an assistant, as `Agent:model`)
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fI<DATE>\fR
The day the work was done (YYYY\-MM\-DD, default: today)
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
The web page of the item the note is about (a PR, bug or Bodhi update); leave it out for work no report lists
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Write the note without showing it first
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITEXT\fR>
The note; `\-` reads it from standard input
.SS sandogasa-report notes
\fBsandogasa\-report notes\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
List recorded notes
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<SINCE>\fR
Only notes from this day on (YYYY\-MM\-DD)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<UNTIL>\fR
Only notes up to this day (YYYY\-MM\-DD)
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Only notes about this URL
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS sandogasa-report report
\fBsandogasa\-report report\fR [\fB\-\-period\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-bodhi\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-bts\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-bugzilla\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-forgejo\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-github\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gitlab\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-koji\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pagure\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-sourcehut\fR] [\fB\-\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-detailed\fR]... [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-private\fR] [\fB\-\-unattached\-notes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-domain\fR>
.PP
Generate an activity report across one or more domains
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fI<DOMAIN>\fR
Domain(s) to report on (defined in config)
.TP
\fB\-\-period\fR \fI<PERIOD>\fR
Reporting period (e.g. 2026Q1, 2026H1)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<SINCE>\fR
Start date (inclusive, YYYY\-MM\-DD)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<UNTIL>\fR
End date (inclusive, YYYY\-MM\-DD, default: today)
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
FAS username to report on
.SH SOURCES
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to main config file (domains, groups)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-bodhi\fR
Skip Bodhi queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-bts\fR
Skip Debian bug tracker queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-bugzilla\fR
Skip Bugzilla queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-forgejo\fR
Skip Forgejo/Gitea queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-github\fR
Skip GitHub queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gitlab\fR
Skip GitLab queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-koji\fR
Skip Koji queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pagure\fR
Skip Pagure queries
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-sourcehut\fR
Skip Sourcehut queries
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fI<AXIS>\fR
Add a breakdown grouped this way (repeat or comma\-separate)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
repo: One row per repository, summed across domains and forges
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-detailed\fR
Add detail. Once: counts per repo, project or component under each heading. Twice: the items themselves — every PR, bug, patch and ticket, and every build of a Bodhi update
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of Markdown
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR
Add the notes recorded with `note` in the period: each under the item it is about, the rest in a section of their own
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write output to file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-private\fR
Make a report for your own use: include GitHub work in private repositories and, with \-\-notes, the notes on items the report does not show, those without a URL, and embargoed ones. Without it, the GitHub section keeps to public repositories and a note shows only under an item the report shows (with \-\-json, any item it carries). The other forges\*(Aq sections include private projects your tokens can see either way
.TP
\fB\-\-unattached\-notes\fR \fI<WHAT>\fR
With \-\-notes and \-\-private, what the Markdown report does with the notes no item took (default: [notes] unattached in the config, or include). \-\-json keeps them, marked unattached
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
include: Close the report with them, grouped by where they point
.IP \(bu 2
exclude: Leave them out
.IP \(bu 2
ask: Ask at the terminal; include them without one
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
